        "name": "Wildfire Risk and Progression Modelling (WRaP)",
        "shortName": "WRAP",
        "date": "July 2025",
        "description": "Java/Spring Boot backend for a wildfire spread simulator (cellular automata driven by Rothermel equations) that helps responders decide where to place early-detection systems. The physics engine is validated within ±5% of Andrews (2018) reference values, backed by 100+ tests and a 7-stage CI pipeline. Requirements were grounded in field research at Karura Forest.",
